When Cursor auto-generates a Git commit message:

- Subject must be 50 characters or less.
- Never exceed 72 characters.
- Use imperative mood.
- Use a single-line commit message whenever possible.
- Do not generate commit bodies unless explicitly required.
- Do not mention every changed file.
- Prefer concise summaries.
- Never add Co-authored-by trailers.
- Never include "Made with Cursor", or "generated by" / "created by" /
  equivalent wording when it attributes authorship to a tool, model, or agent.

Examples:

Add JSON report output

Fix empty input handling

Document project bootstrap
